# FABLE-SONNET-NODE-ROOT-20260923-121 (author on the -67/-84 blocker):
# a resolved method name as a path root denotes its occurrence Structure
# -- M\x is the published own cell of method M's field x, observed from
# outside its activation (here, from E, after the call). bump's own
# field val is read back through bump\val after bump() runs, then
# written through bump\val: 9 and observed again -- same cell, not a
# copy, and independent of bump's own local activation state. Every
# read is routed through a declared local rather than embedded in a
# compound expression: `M\x` inside an if-condition currently reaches
# Grok's -120 c-member-access dispatch instead of this one (it resolves
# the same occurrence address, then emits a literal C ".val" member
# access on it rather than the typed load this path needs) -- a real
# interaction between the two tickets' dispatchers, reported, not fixed
# here (out of -121's scope: assignment-position and simple value-
# position reads are what this ticket's fixtures need).
fn: bump () int
    size_t: val 3U
    return: 0

int: r
size_t: got
r: bump()
if: r != 0
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
got: bump\val
if: got != 3U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 95; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
bump\val: 9U
got: bump\val
if: got != 9U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 96; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
